# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the tp4/prefill-2 window (the device-side hand-off of the final step's GDN state; scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it): copy it over
# .github/c2-serving-job.env on a throwaway commit of tp4/prefill-2 and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN, ONE TAG AT A TIME (wait for the run to finish; never cancel a running card job).
# Nothing here names a rig, a card, a host or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time. The jobs are templates only: no tag is pushed from the branch by its author. ORDER.txt has the
# order, the stop rules, the minutes and the read rules.
# ONE IMAGE FOR THE WHOLE WINDOW: C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf2-1 is a PLACEHOLDER for the tag B0 builds from the pushed branch head WITH the K64j-OQ graft (sed -i 's/tp4-pf2-1/<tag>/' *.env). A commit of a file
# the image carries needs a new B0 build and a new tag in every template. This window never stops, starts or hands back the node agent.
# C2_MODEL_REPO / C2_MODEL_REVISION (qwen_c2_checkpoint.py): a smoke job that carries them serves the Swift checkpoint (what production serves) from its own converted-weight directory; the keys are the same
# in every smoke job of this pack, so each pair differs by the profile alone. The prefix steps (AP1, R1, R2) do not forward the selection into their container and serve the base checkpoint: the hand-off moves
# the GDN state of a finished prefill, whose shape and bytes the checkpoint does not change.
# A1 (EXACTNESS of the device-side hand-off on cold prompts, STOP): c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf2-s4-audit, the ship-4 audited twin (every audit of the
# candidate) with QWEN_FAST_PREFILL_HANDOFF=1 and QWEN_FAST_PREFILL_HANDOFF_AUDIT=1, on Swift. Each of the first 8 final steps and every 24th after reads the whole batched
# decode state of all 48 GDN layers before and after the slot write and requires (a) the slot's rows equal to the scratch's host copy byte for byte on every chip and (b)
# every other row unchanged. warmup; coding (one user); parked_turns (eight seats, forty closed-loop turns of 4k to 24k tokens: forty final steps, each a hand-off beside
# seven decoding seats); prefill_ladder_solo (one request at a time at about 4k, 32k, 128k and 254k tokens: four final steps); prefill_few_decoders (one decoding seat
# beside a 120k-token arrival and two beside a 254k one: two more final steps, at 120k and 254k of context, beside seats that wait for them); concurrent8_steady (eight
# users: eight final steps, then the octo rounds, which the lever never touches). READ: c2_smoke_check clean; the lines in the container log: "[PINDIAG] lever N route
# installed: route=1 audit=0 merged=COLD,CHECKPOINT,SCRATCH,PARKED handoff=device audit" once; on the arms "[PINDIAG] prefill handoff engaged mode=device layers=48
# clones=240" once and one "[PF2] handoff mode=device ms=.. read_ms=0.0 clone_ms=.. write_ms=.. layers=48" per final step; on the control one "[PF2] handoff mode=host ms=..
# read_ms=.. write_ms=.. layers=48" per final step and no "engaged" line; no "fell back" line and no program growth after the warm anywhere; "[PINDIAG] prefill handoff
# audit n=<k> exact=True slot=.. layers=48 tensors_checked=.." for n=1..8 and then every 24th final step, NO "audit mismatch", NO "fell back"; the memory ledger's free DRAM
# per chip after the attach (RECORD it: the device path holds the clones of the 240 scratch tensors, about 70 MB a chip (48 layers x 1.4 MB with the fp32 recurrent state),
# until the last layer is written, against the roughly 4 GB the traffic arm keeps free after the first round). ANY failure is NO-GO for the lever and halts the window.
# CHECKPOINT READ (the workflow passes c2_smoke_check.py --expect-checkpoint): the container log holds "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b@b4c84d42903a
# key=... weight_cache=.../weights-ckpt/<key> base_cache=... (the base cache is not read or written)" once, a "weight cache ...: found" line (the cache the Swift window
# built; this pack never builds it) and the worker's "[QWEN-C2] checkpoint bound ..." line; the models answer names ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b. TELEMETRY (C2_TELEMETRY=1,
# scripts/ci/card_telemetry.py): the read-only ARC sidecar samples every chip once a second through the smoke step; the first [TELEMETRY] line must say decode check ok. A
# rate difference that comes with a different loaded AICLK between the arms is the clocks, not the lever. RUN WITH THE CI PAUSED. Duration (estimate): 100 minutes.
C2_CARDS=quad
C2_ACTIONS=reset smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-pf2-1
C2_PROFILE=c2-packed-tp4-8x262k-ship-prefix-levern-w2-er-pf2-s4-audit
C2_MODEL_REPO=ukisai/Swift-1.5-Qwen3.8-27b
C2_MODEL_REVISION=b4c84d42903a8646b25857eb2827288d92ed85a4
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,parked_turns,prefill_ladder_solo,prefill_few_decoders,concurrent8_steady
C2_TELEMETRY=1
C2_BOX_MINUTES=150
